/**
 * AArch64 code generation through a linear intermediate representation on
 * virtual registers with a global register allocator.
 *
 * The elem trees of each block are selected into machine instructions on
 * virtual registers, the live ranges of those are allocated to the physical
 * registers by spill cost, and the result is emitted as the blocks' `Bcode`,
 * which the rest of `codgenx()` lays out and writes as it does the code of
 * the tree code generator. A function using anything not handled here is
 * generated by the tree code generator.
 *
 * Copyright:   Copyright (C) 2026 by The D Language Foundation, All Rights Reserved
 * License:     $(LINK2 https://www.boost.org/LICENSE_1_0.txt, Boost License 1.0)
 * Source:      $(LINK2 https://github.com/dlang/dmd/blob/master/compiler/src/dmd/backend/arm/lir.d, backend/arm/lir.d)
 */

